---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../lib/site';

const aboutDescription = `About ${SITE_TITLE} — one campaign, told by a bard and by the man playing him.`;
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={aboutDescription}>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <div class="container prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">About this book</h1>

    <p>
      Five of us played one Dungeons &amp; Dragons campaign over Discord, each alone in a
      different room — four players and the DM. One of them kept notes in character, at the table, as it
      happened — a hundred and thirty-eight pages of them, in the first person, written by
      a dwarf bard called Noct who thinks rather well of himself.
    </p>

    <p>
      This book is those notes, and what was actually going on in the five rooms at the
      time. Noct tells his half. The man playing Noct tells the other half. They are the
      same “I”, and they do not always agree.
    </p>

    <h2>The party</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Noct</strong> — dwarf bard. Narrator, in both directions. Unreliable by profession.</li>
      <li><strong>Shae</strong> — tiefling rogue. Goes first, usually invisibly.</li>
      <li><strong>Merlin</strong> — human mage. Familiars, fog, and a great many magic missiles.</li>
      <li><strong>Torgan</strong> — human barbarian. Rages, takes the hits, falls off things.</li>
      <li><strong>Magnus</strong> — dwarf cleric, run by the DM rather than a player. He came along because the party had almost no healing of their own.</li>
      <li><strong>Garnel Stoneblender</strong> — gnome illusionist, found underground at knifepoint, kept as a friend.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The other telling</h2>
    <p>
      The same campaign was run for a younger table, and published as
      <a href="https://ruinsofethium.netlify.app/">The Ruins of Ethium</a> — a Fighting
      Fantasy novel for readers aged twelve and up. Same world, same ruins, same gnome
      rescued from the same tower. Very different evening.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
